In article <91177.143649CERLPDR@TECHNION.BITNET> CERLPDR@TECHNION.BITNET writes:
>  I really hope that this topic can be addressed in 3.1 since IMO it
>is the single most frustrating feature of the game. I'm referring to
>the impossibility of moving past your pet or a friendly monster.
>This is also a real nuscience when moving down a long
>corridor and getting continuous "You stop to avoid hitting your dog"
>messages.
>                            David Rodriguez

I don't think we need any new features here; just set the nosafepet
option and you will be able to attack any of your pets (and you will
still be prompted whether or not you're sure you want to attack your
pet because all pets are peaceful.) I may be wrong, but I think you
can just hit captial 'O' and then enter 'nosafepet' and you can set
the option in the middle of your game (of course this is best set in
nethackoptions). Now this isn't the same as trading places with your
pet, but it still gives you the chance to get past a pet that is
blocking your way if you're willing to kill it.

